diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index d9ac28d..1878e8d 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -26,10 +26,12 @@ Email and password reset link requests use `POST /api/v1/email_verifications` an
 
 Customers register in an active portal with `POST /api/v1/registrations` and a `user` envelope containing `name`, `email`, and `password`. Registration uses the same verification email, login, profile, and password recovery endpoints as staff accounts.
 
-Authenticated customers create and manage their own requests at `POST /api/v1/requests` and `GET/PATCH /api/v1/requests/:id`. `GET /api/v1/requests/:id/comments` lists the conversation. Staff can read and update all account tickets through the corresponding `/tickets` endpoints. Request and ticket updates accept an optional `comment.body` and `status` in their resource envelope.
+Authenticated customers create and manage their own requests at `POST /api/v1/requests` and `GET/PATCH /api/v1/requests/:id`. `GET /api/v1/requests/:id/comments` lists the conversation. Customers can filter their request list with `status`. Staff can read and update all account tickets through the corresponding `/tickets` endpoints. Request and ticket updates accept an optional `comment.body` and `status` in their resource envelope. Staff may also update ticket `priority` (`normal` or `high`); priority is omitted from customer responses and defaults to `normal`.
 
 List endpoints accept `page` and `per_page` (defaults `1` and `25`) and return `count`, `page`, `per_page`, `next_page`, and `previous_page`. Requests and tickets are ordered by recent activity; comments are ordered oldest first.
 
+Staff ticket lists support combined `status`, `priority`, `assignee_id`, and `requester_id` filters plus a case-insensitive `q` search over ticket subjects and public comment text. Set `assignee_id=unassigned` to find tickets without an assignee. Search terms are matched literally, including `%`, `_`, and backslashes.
+
 ## Team invitations and management
 
 Admins can create, list, inspect, resend, and revoke staff invitations at `/api/v1/invitations`. Pending invitations are single-use and block customer registration for the same normalized email. Invitation previews and acceptances are available at `/api/v1/invitation_previews` and `/api/v1/invitation_acceptances`; accepted invitees are verified immediately.
